{
 "document": "DEEPMINE_crosslist",
 "created": "2026-08-20",
 "subfamily": "Cross-listing / multi-ticker identical-claim RV: US ADR vs home ordinary, dual-listed-company (DLC) pairs, and same-issuer ADR share-class pairs",
 "verdict": "NOISE. No formula clears the noise bar on the design window even at ZERO cost, and the held-out window agrees. The mechanism is diagnosed, not just asserted: the daily-close cross-listing spread on free data is ~pure measurement noise (lag-1 autocorrelation of the spread change = -0.49 against a theoretical -0.50 for iid error), so its mean reversion is the reversion of the quote error itself and is not present in any price that can be transacted.",
