   "CA": 49,
   "BR": 102,
   "MX": 91,
   "UK": 88,
   "EU": 102,
   "JP": 153,
   "HK": 312,
   "AR": 211
  },
  "reading": "Canada is the cleanest possible test -- TSX and NYSE open and close the same minute, the listings are fully fungible -- and its spread still measures 49 bp of daily change with rho1 = -0.49. The true premium of a fungible interlisted pair moves by single-digit bp. The free daily feed therefore cannot see the effect at all; it sees its own error. Argentina at -0.18 is the one bloc with a genuinely persistent premium component (the contado-con-liqui FX-control channel), and its costs (182 bp a rebalance) bury it anyway."
 },
